The Rabin-Karp algorithm is a string searching algorithm that uses hashing to find any one of a set of pattern strings in a text.

It works by calculating the hash value of the pattern string and then sliding a window of the same length as the pattern over the text and calculating the hash value of each substring. If the hash values match, it performs a character-by-character comparison to confirm that it's an actual match.

This implementation includes:

